Select a compatible NVENC SDK implementation at runtime

Compile FFmpeg's NVENC implementation against SDK 11.0, 12.0, 13.0,
and 13.1 headers. Query the installed driver's maximum
NVENC API version before encoder initialization and dispatch every encoder
operation to the newest compatible implementation.

NVENC structures and feature fields change between SDK generations, so
rewriting only the API bits in structure version values is not sufficient.
Keeping each implementation isolated behind the existing FFmpeg encoder
interface preserves the correct ABI while allowing one libavcodec build to
run on drivers from the SDK 11.0 generation onward.

